WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
video file & English subtitles: Safex

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.336
Stear, you are thinking about the war
even on a picnic!

00:00:12.013 --> 00:00:16.109
Patty, we are supposed to be happy today.

00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:22.919
Stear insisted on going to war in Europe.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.293
However, after Candy and Mr. Albert
tried to talk him out of it,

00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:28.389
he finally started to doubt his decision.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:35.558
A Cupid with wrinkles.

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:50.246
Sorry!

00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:57.423
Candy, here!

00:00:57.691 --> 00:01:01.095
Sorry, there was an emergency.

00:01:01.295 --> 00:01:04.687
I just got here, too. I got lost.

00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:07.935
It's not polite to let the host wait!

00:01:08.135 --> 00:01:11.831
Right! It's Patty's treat today!

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.270
This restaurant has good food.

00:01:15.709 --> 00:01:16.777
Of course!

00:01:16.977 --> 00:01:20.114
Mr. Albert works part-time here every day.

00:01:20.314 --> 00:01:23.951
Why aren't there any people serving us?

00:01:24.151 --> 00:01:25.486
Yeah.

00:01:25.686 --> 00:01:27.088
I said ''no!''

00:01:27.288 --> 00:01:29.023
What happened?

00:01:29.223 --> 00:01:30.954
I really can't take it.

00:01:31.225 --> 00:01:33.853
I cannot accept something like this.

00:01:34.161 --> 00:01:37.298
Grandmother, are you kidding me?

00:01:37.498 --> 00:01:41.264
Kidding you?
I said I don't want it.

00:01:41.836 --> 00:01:46.040
You must be kidding.
I have hired many workers.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.844
You are the first one
who doesn't want any pay.

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:52.143
I can't take the money.
I work for fun, not for money.

00:01:52.346 --> 00:01:56.840
Right! I should thank you for this!

00:01:57.518 --> 00:01:59.042
What?

00:02:03.157 --> 00:02:05.125
That grandmother...

00:02:05.693 --> 00:02:07.194
Grandmother?

00:02:07.394 --> 00:02:10.024
Maybe I am wrong.

00:02:11.065 --> 00:02:14.696
You must be wrong.
Patty's grandmother is very rich.

00:02:15.503 --> 00:02:19.098
Come on, Grandmother!
Please take it.

00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:20.808
Grandmother.

00:02:21.008 --> 00:02:22.432
Patty.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.713
Boss, I have something to do,
I got to go now!

00:02:25.913 --> 00:02:28.179
- Grandmother!
- The pay!

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:38.789
She started working here a month ago?

00:02:39.793 --> 00:02:42.318
You didn't notice at all?

00:02:42.963 --> 00:02:46.133
She always said she was going
to have tea at her friends'.

00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:48.618
She helped me a lot.

00:02:48.818 --> 00:02:51.068
Since you are her grand daughter...

00:02:53.674 --> 00:02:55.376
It's so troublesome!

00:02:55.576 --> 00:02:57.910
Patty, take it.

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:05.114
Great, I am going to get prepared!

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.496
That was yummy!

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.498
Thank you for the treat, Patty.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:21.782
It's my pleasure.
You helped me convince Stear.

00:03:21.982 --> 00:03:23.899
Patty, you are so sweet!

00:03:24.099 --> 00:03:25.568
It is not true.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:29.313
I'll treat you
when I receive my pay.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.303
Candy, it's my treat next time.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:34.551
I have a job.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:39.244
You are going to Broadway,
you should save the money for it.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:40.954
Annie...

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:43.962
You will see Terry soon.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.716
Come on.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:59.169
Patty and I will take a carriage
from here. Be careful.

00:03:59.369 --> 00:04:00.741
Patty, what's wrong?

00:04:00.941 --> 00:04:02.249
Wait a minute.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.548
Patty, that grandmother...

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.344
- Seems to be Grandmother.
- No way.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:16.048
Grandmother is really healthy!
Take it easy, don't get too tired.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.658
You worry too much.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.124
Excuse me...

00:04:21.528 --> 00:04:23.393
Candy!

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.792
Long time no see!

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:29.764
You, too.
Thanks for taking care of me in London.

00:04:29.964 --> 00:04:31.403
Grandmother!

00:04:31.805 --> 00:04:35.737
Patty! Why are you with Candy?

00:04:35.937 --> 00:04:37.776
Good evening, Grandmother!

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.480
Annie is here, too. It's so rare!

00:04:42.249 --> 00:04:44.183
Grandmother!

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:48.619
Coming!
Excuse me, I have to work.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:56.057
Grandmother, why do you work?

00:04:56.996 --> 00:05:01.868
For my own interest.
Hard work feels rewarding.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:04.960
Do you want to try?

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:08.468
If dad in London finds out about this...

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:12.709
This is America, a free country.

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:20.517
I am going to work now, excuse me.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.686
We just solved Stear's problem.

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:25.752
Now it's Grandmother...

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.193
This is shocking to me.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.992
That grandmother
who took over my shift?

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:38.530
When we were in London, she went
to school and wanted to register.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.964
Will Candy become like that
when she gets old?

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:44.557
Mr. Albert!

00:05:45.057 --> 00:05:48.639
Sorry. She is too old to go to work.

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.764
That's true.
Of course Patty is worried.

00:05:51.964 --> 00:05:54.512
Ok, I am going to convince her
tomorrow.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.688
Please!

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:19.839
Good morning, Candy.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:21.710
Candy?

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:23.979
Grandmother!

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:27.887
From now on,
I'll be working in this hospital.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.322
How do you do!

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:32.016
In this hospital...
How about the other places?

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:36.329
I'll leave for the restaurant
in the evening,

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.294
and pave the road at night.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.532
When do you sleep?

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:44.927
Candy, old people only need
four hours of sleep.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:48.741
No, you will be too tired!

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:52.044
No problem.
Working is the secret to long life.

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:56.012
Candy, let's work hard together today!

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:05.749
Thank you for all the work.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.555
- Wait!
- What?

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:12.526
What did you say?

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:16.083
Thank you for all the work.

00:07:16.283 --> 00:07:21.540
So I heard it right.
You are very polite.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.009
You don't have to thank me for this.

00:07:24.209 --> 00:07:28.045
No. It's not easy to
have a young person like you.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.522
Here, a tip for you.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.654
I can't.

00:07:35.854 --> 00:07:37.623
A little something
to show my appreciation.

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:39.782
- It's not necessary.
- Grandmother!

00:07:40.592 --> 00:07:43.789
Candy, work is wonderful!

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:50.565
You had to work from a young age.
You must feel blessed.

00:07:51.203 --> 00:07:54.070
Grandmother has never worked before?

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:59.610
I couldn't even step out of the door,
let alone work

00:08:04.316 --> 00:08:06.716
My marriage was
my parents’ decision, too.

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:13.356
I was like a bird in a cage.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.323
How about now?

00:08:15.523 --> 00:08:18.588
I was so lucky
to come to America with Patty.

00:08:19.364 --> 00:08:21.992
Right! We can have lunch together!

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.251
Let's eat!

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:42.146
It's so much food here!

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:48.025
I got to eat plenty.
I have three jobs, you know.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.421
Patty is very worried about you.

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:52.397
She is a chicken.

00:08:52.897 --> 00:08:55.500
Candy, I heard you have a boyfriend.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.124
Grandmother!

00:08:58.003 --> 00:09:00.335
I heard he is in New York.

00:09:01.806 --> 00:09:03.336
Why don't you go visit him?

00:09:03.536 --> 00:09:05.376
I'll visit him next month.

00:09:05.576 --> 00:09:08.012
Why didn't he come to see you?

00:09:08.212 --> 00:09:10.672
Terry is preparing for a play.

00:09:11.549 --> 00:09:14.416
You parted because of work.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:18.684
Chicago and New York
are one thousand miles away.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.492
But that shouldn't be a reason
for not seeing each other.

00:09:21.692 --> 00:09:23.526
Soon, the vacation is coming.

00:09:25.129 --> 00:09:27.222
Let me help you.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.763
Wait, Doctor!

00:09:32.904 --> 00:09:37.364
I don't want to tip you.
I have a small favour to ask.

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:39.507
A small favour?

00:09:39.707 --> 00:09:43.579
Which city is halfway
Chicago and New York?

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:45.405
Probably...

00:09:46.651 --> 00:09:49.454
Pittsburgh in Pennsylvania.

00:09:49.654 --> 00:09:53.053
Pittsburgh.
You could meet there, Candy.

00:09:53.253 --> 00:09:54.316
I...

00:09:54.759 --> 00:09:56.227
You will leave from Chicago.

00:09:56.427 --> 00:09:58.696
Terry will go to Pittsburgh
from New York.

00:09:58.896 --> 00:10:03.631
Two people will meet at one place.
It's so romantic!

00:10:03.935 --> 00:10:05.163
Grandmother....

00:10:05.603 --> 00:10:07.772
Wire a telegram to Terry now.

00:10:07.972 --> 00:10:09.407
When do you have a vacation?

00:10:09.607 --> 00:10:12.022
But Terry might not have the time.

00:10:12.222 --> 00:10:14.879
If you always hesitate,
you will never get things done.

00:10:15.079 --> 00:10:17.004
Listen to me!

00:10:20.651 --> 00:10:23.017
A telegram is not convenient.

00:10:23.554 --> 00:10:25.613
I'll send Patty there.

00:10:26.124 --> 00:10:27.525
Patty, to Broadway?

00:10:27.725 --> 00:10:30.361
Yeah, she has a lot of free time.

00:10:30.561 --> 00:10:31.663
But...

00:10:31.863 --> 00:10:37.168
It's ok. I feel younger.

00:10:37.368 --> 00:10:41.034
Let me be Cupid for you two!

00:11:07.198 --> 00:11:10.224
I'm supposed to go to New York alone?

00:11:10.634 --> 00:11:14.126
Isn't it great to travel by train
all day long?

00:11:14.505 --> 00:11:16.996
Grandmother,
can I ask Annie to go with me?

00:11:17.475 --> 00:11:19.773
Patty, how old are you?

00:11:20.244 --> 00:11:22.303
I am the same age as Candy and Annie.

00:11:22.713 --> 00:11:26.684
Listen! Candy went
all the way to England alone.

00:11:27.184 --> 00:11:28.682
- But...
- Patty!

00:11:28.882 --> 00:11:32.687
Don't be a bird in the cage, like me.

00:11:34.091 --> 00:11:35.456
Come in, please.

00:11:36.126 --> 00:11:38.793
Miss Candice White is here.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:41.191
Candy!

00:11:42.132 --> 00:11:43.167
Sorry to bother you.

00:11:43.567 --> 00:11:45.958
We were just talking about you.
Have a seat.

00:11:47.771 --> 00:11:51.809
I have been thinking, and...

00:11:52.259 --> 00:11:54.061
You don't want to see Terry?

00:11:54.261 --> 00:11:58.291
No, but Terry is preparing
for the play.

00:11:58.498 --> 00:12:00.796
Would it be better
that Patty visit Terry?

00:12:01.034 --> 00:12:03.428
Then Patty would know
how Terry is doing.

00:12:03.971 --> 00:12:05.529
Although it sounds right...

00:12:06.707 --> 00:12:09.767
Don't hesitate anymore.

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:13.409
Patty, take the first train
to New York tomorrow.

00:12:13.614 --> 00:12:14.911
Grandmother...

00:12:15.349 --> 00:12:19.308
I'll go to the station
to purchase the ticket before work.

00:12:20.888 --> 00:12:22.823
Patty, you are going alone...

00:12:23.123 --> 00:12:25.426
I can manage.

00:12:25.826 --> 00:12:27.027
Patty.

00:12:27.227 --> 00:12:29.997
Good! That's my girl!

00:12:30.197 --> 00:12:32.531
But, Grandmother,
you have to promise one thing.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:35.281
Spending money? No problem.

00:12:35.481 --> 00:12:37.818
You will not work anymore.

00:12:38.122 --> 00:12:41.603
How could you deprive me
of my hobby?

00:12:41.803 --> 00:12:44.056
I agree with Patty.

00:12:44.294 --> 00:12:45.708
Candy, you too....

00:12:46.008 --> 00:12:49.660
You will be tired out by three jobs.

00:12:50.267 --> 00:12:53.236
You wouldn't make me quit all three?

00:12:53.504 --> 00:12:56.200
Just one of them.

00:12:56.507 --> 00:13:00.811
Alright, as long
as Patty completes the task.

00:13:01.011 --> 00:13:03.004
Really?

00:13:04.148 --> 00:13:05.706
Deal!

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.593
Patty, don't put too much pressure
on Terry.

00:13:16.793 --> 00:13:20.754
You don't need to do this.
Patty is very thoughtful.

00:13:21.031 --> 00:13:24.194
Don't worry, Candy,
please take care of Grandmother.

00:13:24.434 --> 00:13:27.130
I'll take care of myself.

00:13:27.504 --> 00:13:28.806
Good-bye!

00:13:29.006 --> 00:13:30.373
Be careful on the road.

00:13:34.144 --> 00:13:35.372
Patty.

00:13:36.413 --> 00:13:37.437
Candy.

00:13:38.348 --> 00:13:39.337
Patty...

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.989
It's getting romantic!

00:13:48.625 --> 00:13:52.061
Candy, you haven't been to Pittsburgh,
have you?

00:13:53.897 --> 00:13:55.865
Terry must have not been there neither.

00:13:56.065 --> 00:13:59.703
Very soon, two sweethearts
will meet in a foreign city.

00:13:59.903 --> 00:14:01.464
It's so romantic!

00:14:12.182 --> 00:14:13.274
Terry.

00:14:14.116 --> 00:14:17.347
I never thought
we could meet a month earlier,

00:14:18.688 --> 00:14:21.316
between Chicago and New York.

00:14:25.194 --> 00:14:27.897
Why are you smiling, Candy?

00:14:28.197 --> 00:14:30.166
Any good news?

00:14:30.366 --> 00:14:33.536
Nothing.
I am going to take the temperature.

00:14:33.736 --> 00:14:35.571
You forgot the thermometers.

00:14:35.771 --> 00:14:37.696
Oh my!

00:14:46.349 --> 00:14:48.840
Grandmother, why did you fall asleep?

00:14:49.118 --> 00:14:52.110
Grandmother, what's wrong?

00:14:52.989 --> 00:14:56.117
Nothing, I just don't feel well...

00:15:03.933 --> 00:15:06.636
She still has two jobs?

00:15:07.036 --> 00:15:10.918
Yes. Dish washer in a restaurant
and paving worker.

00:15:11.118 --> 00:15:13.337
- Paving worker?
- Yes.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:17.108
Can she do such labouring jobs?

00:15:17.613 --> 00:15:19.382
She is enthusiastic.

00:15:19.582 --> 00:15:22.418
Idiot! Are you really a nurse?

00:15:22.618 --> 00:15:24.319
I have talked to her about this, but...

00:15:24.987 --> 00:15:29.014
If she had done a medical check-up,
things would not be as bad.

00:15:29.859 --> 00:15:31.690
The doctor is right.

00:15:31.894 --> 00:15:36.627
Although she likes to work,
I should have stopped her.

00:15:39.402 --> 00:15:42.462
Notify her family as soon as possible.

00:15:42.872 --> 00:15:44.307
Is it that bad?

00:15:44.507 --> 00:15:45.806
She is old.

00:15:53.249 --> 00:15:54.841
I am sorry, Grandmother.

00:15:55.518 --> 00:15:58.009
I am even a nurse.

00:16:19.775 --> 00:16:21.640
How is Grandmother?

00:16:22.411 --> 00:16:25.347
The telegram for Patty
should have got there.

00:16:25.547 --> 00:16:28.779
It takes three days
for a round trip to New York.

00:16:29.118 --> 00:16:33.489
Candy, Patty can see the telegram
on the way.

00:16:33.689 --> 00:16:36.216
She should be close to Pittsburgh.

00:16:36.492 --> 00:16:37.857
Pittsburgh...

00:16:44.633 --> 00:16:48.125
That's where Terry and I should meet.
Patty...

00:17:00.782 --> 00:17:04.920
Archie, the train seems to be delayed.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.755
Was there an accident?

00:17:06.955 --> 00:17:08.823
No, it seems like the train broke down.

00:17:09.057 --> 00:17:10.808
Why at this moment?

00:17:11.326 --> 00:17:13.802
Archie, let's drive there.

00:17:14.162 --> 00:17:15.461
Let's go!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.643
If she remains longer in a coma...

00:17:27.843 --> 00:17:30.606
Doctor, please try to help Grandmother!

00:17:31.146 --> 00:17:34.638
I can only hope she will wake up soon.

00:17:34.983 --> 00:17:38.077
You didn't sleep all night?

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.480
I am ok.

00:17:44.026 --> 00:17:47.129
Brother, drive safely.

00:17:47.329 --> 00:17:48.992
Be careful not to bite your tongue.

00:17:57.973 --> 00:17:59.099
Grandmother...

00:18:01.076 --> 00:18:03.544
Patty...

00:18:03.779 --> 00:18:06.407
She's coming. Patty is almost here.

00:18:07.616 --> 00:18:10.881
- Patty...
- Hang in there, Grandmother!

00:18:17.993 --> 00:18:19.119
Grandmother!

00:18:23.431 --> 00:18:24.728
Hurry!

00:18:28.136 --> 00:18:29.204
Grandmother!

00:18:29.404 --> 00:18:32.205
Grandmother, Patty is back!

00:18:32.974 --> 00:18:35.043
Grandmother, hang in there!

00:18:35.243 --> 00:18:37.668
Doctor, the pulse is getting faster!

00:18:38.046 --> 00:18:39.911
Prepare for injection!

00:18:46.654 --> 00:18:50.021
Don't make it difficult for us,
please come for visit tomorrow.

00:18:50.892 --> 00:18:55.363
Grandmother is dying, how can we wait?

00:18:55.563 --> 00:18:56.631
Right.

00:18:56.831 --> 00:18:58.858
Quiet! This is a hospital!

00:18:59.501 --> 00:19:01.569
Miss, what happened to Grandmother?

00:19:01.769 --> 00:19:03.571
She has regained her consciousness.

00:19:03.771 --> 00:19:06.731
Really? Grandmother, hang in there!

00:19:07.876 --> 00:19:11.141
Quiet, this is a hospital!

00:19:14.983 --> 00:19:18.111
I won't die.

00:19:18.853 --> 00:19:22.254
Hang in there!

00:19:24.926 --> 00:19:26.209
Grandmother...

00:19:26.409 --> 00:19:30.422
Why did you come back?

00:19:30.765 --> 00:19:32.667
- Because...
- Grandmother.

00:19:32.867 --> 00:19:34.359
I am fine.

00:19:35.437 --> 00:19:37.564
It's my fault.

00:19:38.239 --> 00:19:41.209
No, I don't regret anything.

00:19:41.409 --> 00:19:46.110
Because of work,
I got to know those friends.

00:19:47.382 --> 00:19:48.850
That's great, Patty!

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.281
Thank you.

00:19:50.618 --> 00:19:53.587
Sorry, Candy.
I got off the train in Pittsburgh.

00:19:55.623 --> 00:19:58.114
But I saw Terry in Pittsburgh.

00:19:58.593 --> 00:19:59.855
Terry?

00:20:00.361 --> 00:20:02.192
You'll understand when you go home.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:03.732
Go home?

00:20:03.932 --> 00:20:05.390
Let's go, Candy!

00:20:06.468 --> 00:20:08.561
Grandmother is alright now.

00:20:10.305 --> 00:20:11.294
Ok!

00:20:15.276 --> 00:20:18.768
She saw Terry in Pittsburgh?
Can it be that...

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:24.784
- I am back!
- Welcome home!

00:20:25.586 --> 00:20:27.054
Terry is waiting for you.

00:20:27.254 --> 00:20:28.781
Terry?

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:32.484
Terry, where are you?

00:20:35.296 --> 00:20:36.558
Terry...

00:20:40.968 --> 00:20:42.560
Romeo and Juliet.

00:20:43.738 --> 00:20:45.806
Terry is so cool!

00:20:46.006 --> 00:20:49.865
Patty found this poster
in the lounge in Pittsburgh.

00:20:50.311 --> 00:20:52.939
She really met Terry.

00:20:56.917 --> 00:20:59.520
Candy forgot everything.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:02.555
She's just staring at Terry
in the poster.

00:21:05.993 --> 00:21:07.051
Terry...

00:21:08.329 --> 00:21:10.264
She is concentrating on it so much

00:21:10.464 --> 00:21:13.356
as if she is walking into the poster.

00:21:14.902 --> 00:21:20.067
But, Susanna, the girl in Terry's arms,

00:21:20.374 --> 00:21:22.865
makes Candy hesitate.
